The Ministry for Local Government and Chieftaincy Affairs oversees the operations of all Local Governments and Chieftaincy Institution in the State.
It is important to emphasize that the Ministry is charged with the responsibilities of inspecting, monitoring, providing technical assistance, guidance and advising Local Governments on administration and financial matters as well as coordinating the activities of the 17 Local Government Councils of the State for the realization of their statutory functions and objectives.
Other functions of the Ministry include advising the State Government on policy issues, Chieftaincy matters, public complaints/petition relating to land, boundary and Chieftaincy disputes.
The Ministry is headed by the Hon. Commissioner who is the political Head/Chief Executive, while the Permanent Secretary is the Chief Administrative Officer as well as Chief Accounting Officer of the Ministry. There are Seven (7) Departments as follows:
(i) Administration Department;
(ii) Local Government Inspectorate Department;
(iii) Department of Finance and Supplies;
(iv) Department of Chieftaincy Affairs;
(v) Primary Health Care Department;
(vi) Planning, Research and Statistics; and
(vii) Internal Audit.
Furthermore, the Ministry has 5 Zonal Inspectorate Offices spread across the 17 LGCs as follows:
(i) Jos Zonal Inspectorate Office;
(ii) Shendam Zonal Inspectorate Office;
(iii) Barkin Ladi Zonal Inspectorate Office;
(iv) Langtang Zonal Inspectorate Office; and
(v) Pankshin Zonal Inspectorate Office.
There are two Units headed by Officers posted from the Ministry of Information and Office of the Accountant-General namely: Information Unit and JAAC Accountant

Plateau State Energy Corporation Board (PSEC) was established in 2019, the law was reviewed in 2023, amended and re-enacted 5th March 2024 (Law No. 2, Plateau State House of Assembly). His Excellency the Executive Governor of Plateau State, Barr Caleb Manasseh Mutfwang constituted the Board of the Corporation on February 17, 2025 after carefully assembling competent experts to drive his dreams of the corporation.
Objectives
"The objectives of the Corporation are to:
(a) ensure the development of the State's Energy Resources with diversified energy options for the achievement of the State's energy security and an efficient energy delivery system with optimal energy resources mix;
(b) guarantee increased contribution of energy productive activities to State income;
(c) guarantee adequate, reliable and sustainable supply of energy at appropriate costs, and in an environmentally friendly manner, to the various sectors of the economy for State development;
(d) guarantee an efficient and cost-effective consumption pattern of energy resources;
(e) accelerate the process of acquisition and diffusion of technology and managerial expertise in the Energy Sector and indigenous participation in the Energy Sector industries for stability and self-reliance;
(f) promote investments increased and development of the Energy Sector industries with substantial private sector participation;
(g) ensure a comprehensive, integrated and well- informed energy sector plans and programmes for effective development;
(h) foster national co- operation in energy trade and projects development in the State and nationwide;
(i) successfully use the State's abundant resources to promote national cooperation in the field of energy;
(j) liaise with national and international organizations on energy matters for the development of the energy sector;
(k) collate, analyze and publish information relating to the field of energy from all sources, where such information is related to the discharge of the functions of the Corporation; and invest in the energy sector in all its sources and forms.


Core Values:


L.I.G.H.T.
L - Leadership in Sustainability (Commitment to reducing environmental impact and promoting renewable energy)


I - Integrity (Upholding honesty, transparency, and fairness in all interactions)


G - Growth through Innovation (Encouraging creativity and development to drive growth)


H - Helping the Community (Fostering social responsibility and contributing to local development)


T - Trust and Transparency (Building trust with stakeholders through transparent operations)

ABOUT PLATEAU STATE MINERALS DEVELOPMENT COMPANY LIMITED (PMDC)


PMDC Ltd is a Solid Mineral Processing, Beneficiating, and Exploration company established in 1994 as a Special Purpose Vehicle by the Plateau State
Government. The company's primary mission is to promote economically viable and technically feasible mineral-based projects within the state, driving revenue generation and economic growth. These projects are realized through public-private partnerships with interested investors.


PMDC Ltd is governed by a high-powered Board of Directors responsible for policy-making, supported by a robust management team led by the Managing Director. The company boasts a skilled workforce that includes geologists, geophysicists, engineers, economists, accountants, and administrators, all working together to achieve the company’s objectives.


OBJECTIVES
To acquire mining rights and titles for the Company’s operations;
To explore, exploit and process minerals that are available in Nigeria particularly Plateau State;
To process, refine, reduce and extract raw materials and minerals to their finish and/or semi-finish products;
To stimulate export potentials where raw materials of the State could reach international markets
To offer Consultancy services, geological survey and research in the mineral sector;
To carry on the business of commission agents on mineral products/services, and to sell, import and export both refined and raw minerals;
To manufacture and deal in other goods and services and things of such nature that can in the opinion of the Company be conveniently manufactured or dealt in by the foregoing business.
